HIVE-FSA-005 — Project Helix: The Double Concealment

Difficulty: Expert / Very Difficult
Category: File Signature Analysis, File Header Analysis, OOXML Analysis, Email Forensics, MIME Analysis, Base64 Recovery, Embedded Object Recovery
Flags: 2

Scenario

HIVE CONSULT is conducting an internal investigation following indications that confidential client information may have been removed from an internal evidence repository.
During the investigation, examiners recover a file from an employee workstation named:
Executive_Board_Update.doc
The employee claims that the file contains nothing more than routine executive meeting notes.
When opened normally, the document appears legitimate. It contains HIVE CONSULT branding, meeting notes, governance updates, and a statement indicating that there are no incident-response attachments associated with the document.
However, HIVE's incident-response team received intelligence suggesting that an important email relating to the incident had been deliberately concealed inside the document.
Investigators also believe that the concealed email contains another evidence object that must be recovered separately.
The objective is to locate two independent flags.
